      "text": "According to the triangle angle sum theorem, the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is $180^\\circ$. For $\\triangle ABC$, knowing that $\\angle ABC = 130^\\circ$ and $\\angle BAC = 93^\\circ$, we can find $\\angle ACB$ as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - \\angle ABC - \\angle BAC\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given angle measurements:\n\n\\[\n\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - 130^\\circ - 93^\\circ\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\angle ACB = 57^\\circ\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the measure of $\\angle ACB$ is $\\boxed{57}$ degrees.",
